# lifegame — line-ending and binary policy.
#
# The documentation rules require LF in every text file, so the repository
# normalises on the way in and checks out LF on every platform. Without this,
# a Windows checkout would reintroduce CRLF and the documentation gate would
# fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the change.
#
# Authority: docs/DOCUMENTATION_RULES.md §12, docs/AI_DOCUMENTATION_GUIDE.md §7.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Gate fixtures deliberately contain CRLF pairs, a BOM and a lone CR. Git must
# not normalise them: a normalised fixture stops testing the rule it exists for,
# and the failure would only appear on a fresh clone.
tools/documentation/tests/fixtures/** -text

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.zip binary
*.7z binary
*.mp4 binary
